[h1]Doubt Together (Co-op)[/h1]
Co-op multiplayer for Shadows of Doubt over Steam: one player hosts their sandbox world, a friend joins it, and both work the same cases in the same city. Same evidence, same citizens, same clock.

[b]Works on Windows and on Linux / Steam Deck (Proton). Both players need this item subscribed, in the same version.[/b]

[h2]What's shared[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Case work:[/b] evidence and facts, the case board (pins, strings, notes), objectives, hand-in and verdict. What one player finds counts for both.
[*][b]The world:[/b] doors, locks, switches, items (pick up, drop, throw), alarms, blood, weather, deaths.
[*][b]The city:[/b] the host simulates it, so both see the same people in the same places. Citizens react to both players; fights and damage go both ways.
[*][b]Time:[/b] one clock. It speeds up only when everyone rests; a knocked-out partner never skips your time.
[*][b]Your partner:[/b] a full character in the world. You see them, hear their footsteps, and can watch them in third person while you recover from a knock-out.
[/list]
Money and inventory stay per player.

[h2]Setup (once, both players)[/h2]
[list=1]
[*]Subscribe to this item.
[*]Steam > Shadows of Doubt > Properties > [b]Launch options[/b]: paste the one line for your system (Steam has separate fields per OS):
[code]"..\..\workshop\content\986130\__ITEM_ID__\SoDCoop.cmd" & %command%[/code]
Linux / Steam Play (Proton) / Steam Deck:
[code]sh "../../workshop/content/986130/__ITEM_ID__/SoDCoop.sh" %command%[/code]
[*]Start the game. The [b]first[/b] start takes a few minutes longer (dark window): the loader prepares itself for this game version. Let it finish once.
[*]Host: load a [b]sandbox[/b] save, press F11 (or the Host Co-op button in the main menu). The friend sees the host as "Join <name>" in their main menu, or right-clicks them in the Steam friends list > Join game. Ctrl+Delete leaves the session.
[/list]

[h2]How it works[/h2]
The game's official workshop support only covers data mods, so this item delivers a code mod (BepInEx) the way a few other workshop items do: a small bootstrap script that Steam runs before the game. It copies the bundled loader into the game folder, creating files only where nothing is there yet, so an existing mod-manager setup is never overwritten. Then Steam starts the game as always.
[u]Uninstall[/u]: switch the mod off in the in-game Mods menu and start the game once. The bootstrap then removes the loader's activation files (winhttp.dll, doorstop_config.ini, dotnet\) and the mod DLL from the game folder, and the game starts vanilla. Then unsubscribe and clear the launch option. Loader cache folders (BepInEx\core, unity-libs) stay behind but do nothing; delete them by hand if you want everything gone.

[h2]Notes[/h2]
[list]
[*]Steam has only one launch line: other mods that need launch options have to share it (append with & or ;).
[*]Steam Deck: works out of the box, internal drive or SD card. If nothing happens when you press Play, check in desktop mode that the game folder is writable.
[*]Story mode is not supported (sandbox only). Lobbies are friends-only.
[*]Privacy: everything is peer-to-peer between the two players over Steam, no servers. Your partner sees your Steam name and your character's actions.
[*]Troubleshooting: [b]BepInEx/sodcoop.log[/b] in the game folder tells both players what happened. If something breaks, write in the [b]comments below[/b] or open an [url=https://github.com/0xsimsch/mp_sod/issues]issue on GitHub[/url]. Attach the log from both machines and what you were doing when it happened.
[/list]

